<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23395" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ingressĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		ingredior, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a going into</i>, <i>entering</i>
			(Ciceron.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ab ingressione fori,</span>”
				<i>entrance</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 5, 4, 9</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A gait</i>, <i>pace</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">interdum cursus est in oratione incitatior,
					interdum moderata ingressio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					de Or. 59, 201</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A beginning</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prima ingressio mea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de
					Or. 3, 11</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
